.TH screen 1 "Wed Aug 19 2026"
.SH NAME
screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B screen
[\-abBchLnomrVxk] [\-u delay] [\-C color] [\-t tty] [\-M message]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows a scrolling 'Matrix'-like screen in a Linux terminal console.
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
.I "\-a"
Asynchronous scroll
.TP
.I "\-b"
Bold characters on
.TP
.I "\-B"
All bold characters (overrides \-b)
.TP
.I "\-c"
Use Japanese characters as seen in the original "The Matrix" cinematic film (default)
.TP
.I "\-h, \-?"
Print usage and exit
.TP
.I "\-k"
Characters change while scrolling
.TP
.I "\-L"
Lock mode (can be closed from another terminal)
.TP
.I "\-m"
"Lambda" mode, every character becomes a lambda
.TP
.I "\-M message"
Add a message in the center of 'screen'
.TP
.I "\-n"
No bold characters (overrides \-b and \-B)
.TP
.I "\-o"
Use old-style scrolling
.TP
.I "\-r"
"Rainbow" mode, rainbow colored character
.TP
.I "\-s"
"Screensaver" mode, exits on first keystroke
.TP
.I "\-t tty"
Set tty to use
.TP
.I "\-u delay"
Screen update delay 0 - 10, default 4
.TP
.I "\-V"
Print version information and exit
.TP
.I "\-x"
X window mode, use if your xterm is using mtx.pcf
.TP
.I "\-C color"
Use this color for matrix (default red).
Valid colors are green, red, blue, white, yellow, cyan, magenta and black.
.SS KEYSTROKES
The following keystrokes are available during execution (unavailable in
\-s mode)
.TP
.I "a"
Toggle asynchronous scroll
.TP
.I "b"
Random bold characters
.TP
.I "B"
All bold characters
.TP
.I "m"
Toggle lambda mode
.TP
.I "n"
Turn off bold characters
.TP
.I "p, P"
Pause and unpause the matrix stream
.TP
.I "r"
Toggle rainbow color mode
.TP
.I "0\-9"
Adjust update speed
.TP
.I "! @ # $ % ^ & )"
Change the color of the matrix to the corresponding color:
! \- red, @ \- green, # \- yellow, $ \- blue, % \- magenta, ^ \- cyan,
& \- white, ) \- black.
.TP
.I "q"
Quit the program
.SH BUGS
This program is a fork of 'cmatrix' which is known to be very CPU intensive on older hardware. This is being improved in 'screen'.
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://www.github.com/fpucore/screen
